MiniMax-M3 oracle prompts (tools/ref/minimaxm3-dump.sh): token ids, one decimal id a line, no BOS (the file's add_bos_token is
false, so llama-tokenize adds none). The dumper never tokenizes (tools/ref/cb_dump.cpp): a tokenizer difference would read as a
kernel bug.

Made once, on the box, by the tokenizer of the dump's own tree (mainline llama.cpp cd0a5b6a180dff0048e5fd993098b21c0b2c91b8,
/home/user/llama.cpp-mainline-bolt, CPU build; llama-tokenize md5 f39e6d406cdb6232145cd30a85ca4fb0, libllama.so md5
d846809bb9cd2cb8aa304ed4b9003fed) on the first shard of the UD-IQ4_XS file (vocabulary only):

    llama-tokenize -m <first shard> -f <text> --ids --no-escape --log-disable     # "[id, id, ...]", written one id a line

